# Exercise 6: Comparisons
#
# Numbers are written without quotes: fact age("Ana", 17). You can compare
# them in a rule with < > <= >= == !=
#
#     rule tall(x):
#         height(x, h)
#         AND h > 180
#
# A comparison needs to know both values, so put the goal that finds h
# (height(x, h)) before the comparison that tests it.
#
# Your tasks:
#   1. adult(x): x is 18 or older
#   2. teen(x): x is between 13 and 19, including 13 and 19

fact age("Ana", 17)
fact age("Ben", 30)
fact age("Cy", 12)
fact age("Di", 13)
fact age("Eli", 19)

# Write your rules below this line.



# --- Checks: run ./sova --check on this file. Don't change below here. ---
hint "Start each rule with age(x, a) to find x's age a."
hint "For adult, test a >= 18. For teen, you need two comparisons joined with AND."
expect adult("Ben")
expect NOT adult("Ana")
expect adult(who) gives "Ben", "Eli"
expect teen("Ana")
expect NOT teen("Cy")
expect teen(who) gives "Ana", "Di", "Eli"
